ptures and forks with the same entryId, then packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/fork.test.ts:190-200 asserts target work is pending rather than copied ready state and packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/fork.test.ts:210-225 verifies both threads derive ready forms independently.\"}],\"newFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-04-005\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Fork creation/init failure falls through to normal launch\",\"evidence\":\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:325-330 records fork_thread_creation_failed and then falls through to normal launch resolution; packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:335-340 does the same after fork target init failure. Story AC-3.1 requires a fork to create a new LHC thread, and the real-code workaround standard does not allow replacing a failed fork with an unrelated normal launch path.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-3.1\",\"TC-3.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true}],\"openFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-04-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"PI session-tree fallback is not proven from fork tree evidence\",\"evidence\":\"Story Scope In and TC-3.1 require PI's session tree as Epic 1 fallback evidence when session_before_fork is absent; tech-design Flow 3 specifically names the parentId chain. packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/fork.ts:19-36 uses previousSessionFile and the last id/entryId from current entries or a parsed file, without checking parentId/fork relationship. The current fork tests do not exercise the hook-absent fallback path.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/fork.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/fork.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-3.1\",\"TC-3.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"SV-04-005\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Fork creation/init failure falls through to normal launch\",\"evidence\":\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:325-330 records fork_thread_